 "lines": [
  "The mountain fell on Kai.",
  "Fresh snow. Deep backcountry. Nora, Leo and Kai.",
  "@am_echo: \"Guys... is this slope safe?\"",
  "@am_michael: \"Relax. It's just snow.\"",
  "Most avalanches start on slopes of thirty to forty-five degrees. Like this one.",
  "Crack. The whole slab of snow broke loose under Kai's skis.",
  "Within seconds, a slab avalanche can hit about eighty miles an hour.",
  "Nine out of ten deadly avalanches are set off by the victim, or their own group.",
  "@af_nova: \"Kai! Grab a tree! Swim!\"",
  "Caught? Get to the side, grab a tree, or swim hard to stay up.",
  "As it slows, push a hand up, and clear a space in front of your mouth.",
  "Then it stops. And the snow sets up almost like concrete.",
  "@am_echo: \"I'll go get help!\"",
  "@af_nova: \"No! We're his only chance!\"",
  "Most buried people die from lack of air, and most have less than fifteen minutes.",
  "A rescue team can't get there that fast. So his friends have to.",
  "Everyone's beacon sends a signal. Nora switches hers to search.",
  "@af_nova: \"Signal! He's [close](klohss)!\"",
  "A long probe finds him, about three feet down.",
  "Then the slowest part. Digging.",
  "A hand. A face. The space he cleared kept him breathing.",
  "Dug out within ten minutes or so, most survive. By thirty-five minutes, only about one in three.",
  "@am_echo: \"Still think it's just snow? Not after...\""
 ],
